If C10 visually shows 1 but VBA reads it as empty, one of these is 99% the cause.


---

🔴 WHY THIS HAPPENS

✅ Most common reasons

1. C10 is merged but the value is NOT stored in C10

Excel stores the value in the top-left cell of the merged area

That top-left cell may be B10, C9, or C10 depending on how it was merged



2. C10 contains a formula returning ""

Looks like 1, but VBA reads "" (empty string)



3. C10 is text "1" from a formula but merged area hides it




---

✅ THE REAL FIX (Guaranteed)

🔧 Read the VALUE from the TOP-LEFT CELL of the MERGED AREA

Instead of assuming C10 holds the value, force VBA to read from the merged area’s first cell.


